{
  // The SERVER project: `src/**` (the Node half), the tests that run in the
  // Node environment, and the root config files. Its counterpart is
  // `tsconfig.ui.json`, which owns the UI environment (DOM libs + the JSX
  // transform). The split exists because `lib`/`jsx`/`types` are per-PROJECT
  // settings: compiling the UI files here would resolve `document`, `window`
  // and `react/jsx-runtime` against a lib set that deliberately lacks them.
  //
  // `npm run typecheck` runs BOTH projects, so every file is checked exactly
  // once — the two `include`/`exclude` sets are proven to partition
  // `tests/**/*.test.ts` by `tests/unit/projectCoverage.test.ts`. Change one
  // side and that test fails rather than letting a file go unchecked.
  //
  // `nodenext` is deliberate and differs from `tsconfig.ui.json`'s `bundler`:
  // this project is the Node half and is BUNDLED EMIT-FREE (`noEmit` here,
  // tsdown for `dist/`), so `nodenext` is what makes the typechecker model the
  // real Node ESM resolver the published artifact runs under. The price is the
  // `nodenext` ESM convention: every RELATIVE import must name the emitted
  // `.js` file even though the source is `.ts` (`./tools.js` -> `src/tools.ts`).
  // Bare specifiers (`node:*`, `@cherrystudio/*`, `vitest`, ...) are resolved
  // from `node_modules` unchanged and MUST NOT be suffixed. vitest/vite resolve
  // the `.js`-suffixed relative paths back to the `.ts` sources, so the test
  // run is unaffected. See `docs/` and the fix-d report for the migration.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2023",
    "module": "nodenext",
    "moduleResolution": "nodenext",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "strict": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src", "tests", "vitest.config.ts", "tsdown.config.ts"],
  // `ui/**` and the three UI-environment test files belong to tsconfig.ui.json
  // (see its header — one of the three, `tests/integration/clientBundle.test.ts`,
  // is NOT a jsdom test); `_research/**` is a vendored upstream checkout, not
  // this plugin's source, so it is neither built nor typechecked here.
  "exclude": [
    "ui",
    "tests/unit/i18n.test.ts",
    "tests/unit/ui.test.ts",
    "tests/unit/uiScopePanel.test.ts",
    "tests/integration/clientBundle.test.ts",
    "_research"
  ]
}
